        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: deludere",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "deludere — \"to disappoint, to let down\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il film mi ha deluso: mi aspettavo di più. The film disappointed me: I expected more."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A false friend: it means to disappoint, not to delude. The past participle is deluso."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "deludere is a learned borrowing from Latin dēlūdere \"to make fun of, to deceive\" (Lewis & Short), built on lūdere \"to play\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
